  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Rapid Response for flood-affected people in Bayelsa, Anambra, and Niger States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide health, water sanitation and hygiene (WASH), child protection, and multipurpose cash assistance to vulnerable communities affected by flooding in Nigeria. This UNICEF project provides primary health services to prevent and treat waterborne diseases, distributes WASH supplies, provides safe water and access to sanitation facilities, supports affected children through psychosocial services, strengthens protection from gender-based violence, and provides multipurpose cash. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 145,400 people in the Health sector, 90,000 people in the WASH sector, 8,600 people in the Protection (CP) sector, and 3,500 people with multipurpose cash assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
